{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And HaShem Elohim said to the woman, etc.</b> The reason for this question is for her to confess her sin before HaShem, for through this there would be healing for her affliction, for she said ״הַנָּחָשׁ הִשִּׁיאַנִי״ — and this is her confession. It is also an argument that she was inadvertent in the matter, on account of the serpent's seduction. And I have already written above that she did not know that this seducer existed, for had she known him she would not have listened to him. And her saying <b>הִשִּׁיאַנִי</b> alludes to the language of exalted headship (n'si'ut), for he told her that through this eating she would become like Elohim and be exalted — and she confessed her error before her Maker."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:38:12.310779289Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}